==Icelandic==
{{cardinalbox|is|3|4|5|þrír|fimm|ord=fjórði}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|is|fjór}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|fjórir}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*fedwōr}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*kʷetwṓr}}, the neuter form of {{der|is|ine-pro|*kʷetwóres}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfjouːrir/}}

===Numeral===
{{head|is|numeral|g=m-p|feminine plural|fjórar|neuter plural|fjögur}}

# [[four]]; the cardinal number after {{m|is|þrír||three}} and before {{m|is|fimm||five}}.
#: ''[[sjá|Sjáðu]]! '''Fjórir''' [[maður#Icelandic|menn]].''
#:: [[look|Look]]! '''Four''' [[man|men]].

====Declension====
{{is-numeral (fjórir)|}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|klukkan fjögur}}
* {{l|is|undir fjögur augu}}
* {{l|is|á fjórum fótum}}

====Usage notes====
When counting out loud, the contraction {{m|is|fjór}} is frequently used.

===See also===
* {{l|is|fjarki|pos=n}}

